module

public import StacksFrontier.Homology.DerivedComplete.NoetherianKoszulProIso
import StacksCore.Tactic.EgaSgaAttribute

/-!
# Koszul homology with coefficients is pro-zero in positive degrees

Let `A` be a Noetherian commutative ring, let `f : Fin r → A` be a finite sequence and let `M`
be a finite `A`-module. For every `n` the Koszul complex `K(f₀^{n+1}, …, f_{r-1}^{n+1})` is a
bounded complex of finite free modules, so its tensor product with `M` computes
`M ⊗^𝐋_A K(f₀^{n+1}, …, f_{r-1}^{n+1})`, and the canonical transition maps of
[Stacks, Tag 0BKC] tensor up to a tower of such complexes. This file proves that the induced
maps on homology in every **positive** degree are zero after passing to a sufficiently late
level: the positive Koszul homology of the tower, with coefficients in `M`, is pro-zero.

At `M = A` this is the Noetherian input of [Stacks, Tag 0921],
`NoetherianKoszulProIso.koszulPowerTransition_homologyMap_eq_zero_pos`. The statement proved
here is the same one with coefficients, which is what the Koszul tower
`n ↦ ℱ ⊗^𝐋_{𝒪} K(𝒪, a₁ⁿ, …, a_rⁿ)` of [Stacks, Tags 0A0E and 0A0K] restricts to on an affine
open, at an arbitrary number of generators.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.KoszulCoefficientProIso.rTensorFunctor` — tensoring on the right by a module, as an
  additive endofunctor of the category of modules.
* `Stacks.KoszulCoefficientProIso.rTensorChainFunctor` — the induced endofunctor of chain
  complexes, which carries the Koszul complexes on the powers of `f` to the Koszul complexes
  with coefficients in `M`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.KoszulCoefficientProIso.span_le_annihilator_homology_rTensor` — the ideal generated by
  a sequence annihilates every homology module of its Koszul complex with coefficients. This is
  [Stacks, Tag 0663] with coefficients, obtained by transporting the null-homotopy of
  multiplication along the additive functor.
* `Stacks.KoszulCoefficientProIso.koszulCoefficientTransition_homologyMap_eq_zero_pos` — **the
  Artin–Rees input with coefficients**: over a Noetherian ring, for a finite module `M`, every
  level `n` and every positive degree `j` admit a later level `m` at which the Koszul transition
  map with coefficients in `M` induces the zero map on homology in degree `j`.
* `Stacks.KoszulCoefficientProIso.isIso_homologyMap_zero_rTensor` — an augmentation of a chain
  complex onto a module in degree zero stays an isomorphism on `H₀` after tensoring, because in
  degree zero homology is a cokernel and tensoring is right exact.
* `Stacks.KoszulCoefficientProIso.coefficientKoszulPowerSystem_proIso_quotientPowerSystem` —
  **[Stacks, Tag 0921] with coefficients, at an arbitrary number of generators**: in `D(R)` the
  tower `n ↦ M ⊗^𝐋_R K(R, f₁ⁿ, …, f_rⁿ)` and the tower `n ↦ M ⊗_R R/(f₁ⁿ, …, f_rⁿ)` in degree
  zero are isomorphic as pro-objects. No `@[stacks]` attribute is placed on it: [Stacks, Tag
  0921] is the statement at coefficients in `R`, which
  `NoetherianKoszulProIso.koszulPowerSystem_proIso_quotientPowerSystem` already registers.

## Implementation notes

As in `NoetherianKoszulProIso`, positive powers are indexed by `n : ℕ` using the exponent
`n + 1`, and the Koszul complex is the homological one of `Koszul.seqComplex`.

Coefficients are inserted by the additive endofunctor `- ⊗[A] M` rather than by
`Koszul.seqComplexTensor`, because the two inputs of the argument are both transported along a
functor: the null-homotopy of multiplication by `f i`, through
`CategoryTheory.Functor.mapHomotopy`, and the chain maps of the tower, through
`CategoryTheory.Functor.mapHomologicalComplex`. Both would have to be rebuilt by hand for a
complex defined by `ChainComplex.of`.

The pro-isomorphism in the derived category is assembled from the chain-level statement exactly
as in the coefficient-free case, through [Stacks, Tag 0G3D],
`DerivedCategory.exists_proInverse_of_proInverse_homology`: the two towers have homology only in
the degrees `-r, …, 0`, the comparison is an isomorphism on `H⁰`, and in negative degrees the
source is pro-zero while the target vanishes.

The three general inputs of the argument are used exactly as in the coefficient-free case and
need no generalization: `NoetherianKoszulProIso.artinRees_cycles_bound` (Artin–Rees applied to
the cycles of the complex, which is where the Noetherian hypothesis enters),
`NoetherianKoszulProIso.ideal_smul_ker_le_range_of_annihilator` and
`NoetherianKoszulProIso.shortComplex_homologyMap_eq_zero_of_ideal_range` are all stated for an
arbitrary short complex of modules whose middle term is finite. What does have to be redone with
coefficients is the annihilation of the homology by the ideal and the containment of the image of
the transition map in a power of the ideal.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0663](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0663)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0921](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0921)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A0E](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A0E)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite
open NoetherianKoszulProIso
open scoped TensorProduct

universe u

namespace Stacks.KoszulCoefficientProIso

variable {R : Type u} [CommRing R]

/-! ### Tensoring by a module as an additive functor -/

/-- **Tensoring on the right by a module.** The additive endofunctor `N ↦ N ⊗[R] M` of the
category of `R`-modules; on morphisms it is `LinearMap.rTensor`. -/
noncomputable def rTensorFunctor (M : ModuleCat.{u} R) : ModuleCat.{u} R ⥤ ModuleCat.{u} R where
  obj N := ModuleCat.of R (N ⊗[R] M)
  map {_ _} φ := ModuleCat.ofHom (LinearMap.rTensor M φ.hom)
  map_id _ := ModuleCat.hom_ext <| TensorProduct.ext' fun _ _ => rfl
  map_comp _ _ := ModuleCat.hom_ext <| TensorProduct.ext' fun _ _ => rfl

/-- The functor `N ↦ N ⊗[R] M` is additive. -/
instance (M : ModuleCat.{u} R) : (rTensorFunctor M).Additive where
  map_add {_ _} {φ ψ} := by
    change ModuleCat.ofHom (LinearMap.rTensor M ((φ + ψ).hom)) = _
    rw [show ((φ + ψ).hom) = φ.hom + ψ.hom from rfl, LinearMap.rTensor_add]
    rfl

/-- Tensoring by a module commutes with the scalar multiples of an identity. -/
theorem rTensorFunctor_map_smul_id (M N : ModuleCat.{u} R) (a : R) :
    (rTensorFunctor M).map (a • 𝟙 N) = a • 𝟙 ((rTensorFunctor M).obj N) := by
  change ModuleCat.ofHom (LinearMap.rTensor M ((a • (𝟙 N : N ⟶ N)).hom)) = _
  rw [show ((a • (𝟙 N : N ⟶ N)).hom) = a • (LinearMap.id : N →ₗ[R] N) from rfl,
    LinearMap.rTensor_smul, LinearMap.rTensor_id]
  rfl

/-- **Tensoring a chain complex on the right by a module.** Applied to the Koszul complex of a
finite sequence this is the Koszul complex with coefficients in `M`. -/
noncomputable abbrev rTensorChainFunctor (M : ModuleCat.{u} R) :
    ChainComplex (ModuleCat.{u} R) ℕ ⥤ ChainComplex (ModuleCat.{u} R) ℕ :=
  (rTensorFunctor M).mapHomologicalComplex (ComplexShape.down ℕ)

/-- Tensoring a chain complex by a module commutes with the scalar multiples of an identity. -/
theorem rTensorChainFunctor_map_smul_id (M : ModuleCat.{u} R)
    (K : ChainComplex (ModuleCat.{u} R) ℕ) (a : R) :
    (rTensorChainFunctor M).map (a • 𝟙 K) = a • 𝟙 ((rTensorChainFunctor M).obj K) := by
  refine HomologicalComplex.hom_ext _ _ (fun i => ?_)
  change (rTensorFunctor M).map ((a • (𝟙 K : K ⟶ K)).f i) = _
  rw [show ((a • (𝟙 K : K ⟶ K)).f i) = a • 𝟙 (K.X i) from rfl, rTensorFunctor_map_smul_id]
  rfl

/-! ### The ideal annihilates the Koszul homology with coefficients -/

/-- **Stacks 0663 with coefficients.** The ideal generated by a finite sequence annihilates every
homology module of its Koszul complex with coefficients in an arbitrary module: multiplication by
`f i` is null-homotopic on the Koszul complex, and an additive functor carries a null-homotopy to
a null-homotopy. -/
theorem span_le_annihilator_homology_rTensor {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → R) (M : ModuleCat.{u} R)
    (n : ℕ) :
    Ideal.span (Set.range f) ≤
      Module.annihilator R
        (((rTensorChainFunctor M).obj (Koszul.seqComplex f)).homology n) := by
  refine Ideal.span_le.2 ?_
  rintro a ⟨i, rfl⟩
  refine Module.mem_annihilator.mpr (fun x => ?_)
  have H := Classical.choice
    ((Koszul.koszulSeq_smul_nullHomotopic_and_span_le_annihilator f).1 i)
  have H' : Homotopy ((rTensorChainFunctor M).map (f i • 𝟙 (Koszul.seqComplex f)))
      ((rTensorChainFunctor M).map 0) := (rTensorFunctor M).mapHomotopy H
  rw [(rTensorChainFunctor M).map_zero] at H'
  have hm := H'.homologyMap_eq n
  rw [rTensorChainFunctor_map_smul_id, Koszul.homologyMap_smul_id,
    HomologicalComplex.homologyMap_zero] at hm
  simpa only [ModuleCat.hom_smul, ModuleCat.hom_id, LinearMap.smul_apply, LinearMap.id_apply,
    ModuleCat.hom_zero, LinearMap.zero_apply] using congrArg (fun q => q.hom x) hm

/-! ### The image of a transition map lands in a power of the ideal -/

/-- Tensoring by a module preserves the containment of the image of a map in an ideal multiple of
the target: the image is generated by the elements `φ x ⊗ y`, and `y ↦ x ⊗ y` is linear. -/
theorem range_rTensorFunctor_map_le_smul (M : ModuleCat.{u} R) {P Q : ModuleCat.{u} R}
    (φ : P ⟶ Q) (I : Ideal R) (h : LinearMap.range φ.hom ≤ I • (⊤ : Submodule R Q)) :
    LinearMap.range ((rTensorFunctor M).map φ).hom ≤
      I • (⊤ : Submodule R ((rTensorFunctor M).obj Q)) := by
  rintro z ⟨w, rfl⟩
  change LinearMap.rTensor M φ.hom w ∈ I • (⊤ : Submodule R (Q ⊗[R] M))
  induction w using TensorProduct.inductionOn with
  | tmul p m =>
      rw [LinearMap.rTensor_tmul]
      exact linearMap_mem_ideal_smul_top I ((TensorProduct.mk R Q M).flip m) (h ⟨p, rfl⟩)
  | add a b ha hb =>
      rw [map_add]
      exact Submodule.add_mem _ ha hb

/-- In positive degrees the image of a Koszul transition map lies in any ideal containing the
powers `f i ^ (m - n)` by which it scales the generators. This is the coefficient-free statement,
restated publicly from the data of [Stacks, Tag 0BKC]. -/
theorem koszulPowerTransition_range_le_idealSmul {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → R)
    (m n : ℕ) (hmn : n ≤ m) (q : ℕ) (I : Ideal R) (hf : ∀ i, f i ^ (m - n) ∈ I) :
    LinearMap.range ((koszulPowerTransition f m n hmn).f (q + 1)).hom ≤
      I • (⊤ : Submodule R (⋀[R]^(q + 1) (Fin r → R))) := by
  let L : (⋀[R]^(q + 1) (Fin r → R)) →ₗ[R] (⋀[R]^(q + 1) (Fin r → R)) :=
    ((koszulPowerTransition f m n hmn).f (q + 1)).hom
  change LinearMap.range L ≤ I • (⊤ : Submodule R (⋀[R]^(q + 1) (Fin r → R)))
  have hspan : Submodule.span R
      (Set.range (exteriorPower.ιMulti R (q + 1) :
        (Fin (q + 1) → Fin r → R) → ⋀[R]^(q + 1) (Fin r → R))) ≤
      (I • (⊤ : Submodule R (⋀[R]^(q + 1) (Fin r → R)))).comap L := by
    rw [Submodule.span_le]
    rintro _ ⟨v, rfl⟩
    change L (exteriorPower.ιMulti R (q + 1) v) ∈
      I • (⊤ : Submodule R (⋀[R]^(q + 1) (Fin r → R)))
    have hformula := koszulPowerTransition_apply_ιMulti f m n hmn (q + 1) v
    change L (exteriorPower.ιMulti R (q + 1) v) =
      (⟨ExteriorAlgebra.ιMulti R (q + 1)
        (fun k i => f i ^ (m - n) * v k i), Koszul.ιMulti_mem _ _⟩ :
        ⋀[R]^(q + 1) (Fin r → R)) at hformula
    rw [hformula]
    exact ιMulti_succ_mem_ideal I _ (weighted_vector_mem_ideal I _ _ hf)
  rw [exteriorPower.ιMulti_span] at hspan
  rintro _ ⟨y, rfl⟩
  exact hspan Submodule.mem_top

/-! ### The Artin–Rees input with coefficients -/

/-- **The positive Koszul homology of the power tower, with coefficients in a finite module over
a Noetherian ring, is pro-zero.** For every level `n` and every positive degree `j` there is a
later level `m` at which the Koszul transition map from the `(m+1)`-st to the `(n+1)`-st powers,
tensored with `M`, induces the zero map on homology in degree `j`.

This is [Stacks, Tag 0921]'s Noetherian input with coefficients. In degree `j = q + 1` the
transition map scales the `i`-th generator by `f i ^ (m - n)`, so for `m = n + (n + 1) k` its
image lies in `Jᵏ` times the whole term, where `J` is the ideal generated by the `(n+1)`-st
powers; `J` annihilates the homology, so `J` times the cycles lies in the boundaries, and
Artin–Rees applied to the cycles inside the finite module `⋀^{q+1}(Rʳ) ⊗ M` makes `Jᵏ` times the
term meet the cycles inside the boundaries once `k` is large. -/
@[sga "2 II Lemma11" "special case"]
theorem koszulCoefficientTransition_homologyMap_eq_zero_pos [IsNoetherianRing R]
    {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → R) (M : ModuleCat.{u} R) [Module.Finite R M] (n j : ℕ) (hj : 0 < j) :
    ∃ (m : ℕ) (h : n ≤ m),
      HomologicalComplex.homologyMap
        ((rTensorChainFunctor M).map (koszulPowerTransition f m n h)) j = 0 := by
  cases j with
  | zero => omega
  | succ q =>
    let J : Ideal R := Ideal.span (Set.range fun i => f i ^ (n + 1))
    let K := (rTensorChainFunctor M).obj (Koszul.seqComplex (fun i => f i ^ (n + 1)))
    let T := K.sc (q + 1)
    let : Module.Finite R T.X₂ := by
      change Module.Finite R ((⋀[R]^(q + 1) (Fin r → R)) ⊗[R] M)
      infer_instance
    have hJ : J ≤ Module.annihilator R T.homology :=
      span_le_annihilator_homology_rTensor (fun i => f i ^ (n + 1)) M (q + 1)
    have hJB := ideal_smul_ker_le_range_of_annihilator T J hJ
    obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := artinRees_cycles_bound J
      (LinearMap.ker T.g.hom) (LinearMap.range T.f.hom) hJB
    let m := n + (n + 1) * k
    have hmn : n ≤ m := Nat.le_add_right _ _
    let S := ((rTensorChainFunctor M).obj
      (Koszul.seqComplex (fun i => f i ^ (m + 1)))).sc (q + 1)
    let φ : S ⟶ T :=
      (HomologicalComplex.shortComplexFunctor (ModuleCat R) (ComplexShape.down ℕ) (q + 1)).map
        ((rTensorChainFunctor M).map (koszulPowerTransition f m n hmn))
    have hrange : LinearMap.range φ.τ₂.hom ≤ J ^ k • (⊤ : Submodule R T.X₂) :=
      range_rTensorFunctor_map_le_smul M _ (J ^ k)
        (koszulPowerTransition_range_le_idealSmul f m n hmn q (J ^ k)
          (power_generator_mem_span_pow f n k))
    exact ⟨m, hmn, shortComplex_homologyMap_eq_zero_of_ideal_range S T φ J k hk hrange⟩

/-! ### Degree zero: the coefficient augmentation stays an isomorphism on `H₀` -/

/-- For a chain complex indexed by `ℕ`, being an isomorphism on homology in degree zero and
being one on opcycles in degree zero are the same condition: in degree zero the canonical map
from homology to opcycles is invertible, and it is natural. -/
theorem isIso_opcyclesMap_zero_iff {C D : ChainComplex (ModuleCat.{u} R) ℕ} (φ : C ⟶ D) :
    IsIso (HomologicalComplex.opcyclesMap φ 0) ↔
      IsIso (HomologicalComplex.homologyMap φ 0) := by
  have key := ChainComplex.isoHomologyι₀_inv_naturality φ
  constructor
  · intro h
    have hrw : HomologicalComplex.homologyMap φ 0 = C.isoHomologyι₀.hom ≫
        HomologicalComplex.opcyclesMap φ 0 ≫ D.isoHomologyι₀.inv := by
      rw [← key, Iso.hom_inv_id_assoc]
    rw [hrw]
    infer_instance
  · intro h
    have hrw : HomologicalComplex.opcyclesMap φ 0 = C.isoHomologyι₀.inv ≫
        HomologicalComplex.homologyMap φ 0 ≫ D.isoHomologyι₀.hom := by
      rw [← Category.assoc, key, Category.assoc, Iso.inv_hom_id, Category.comp_id]
    rw [hrw]
    infer_instance

/-- An element of the degree-zero term of a chain complex of modules dies in the opcycles in
degree zero exactly when it is a boundary. -/
theorem pOpcycles_eq_zero_iff_mem_range {C : ChainComplex (ModuleCat.{u} R) ℕ} (x : C.X 0) :
    C.pOpcycles 0 x = 0 ↔ x ∈ LinearMap.range ((C.sc 0).f).hom :=
  ShortComplex.moduleCat_pOpcycles_eq_zero_iff (C.sc 0) x

/-- If the differential into degree zero vanishes, the projection onto the opcycles in degree
zero is injective. -/
private theorem eq_zero_of_pOpcycles_eq_zero {C : ChainComplex (ModuleCat.{u} R) ℕ}
    (hC : (C.sc 0).f = 0) (y : C.X 0) (hy : C.pOpcycles 0 y = 0) : y = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ := (pOpcycles_eq_zero_iff_mem_range y).1 hy
  rw [← hw, hC]
  simp only [ModuleCat.hom_zero, LinearMap.zero_apply]
  rfl

/-- A map of chain complexes onto a complex with zero differential into degree zero which is an
isomorphism on opcycles in degree zero is surjective in degree zero. -/
private theorem surjective_f_zero_of_isIso_opcyclesMap {C D : ChainComplex (ModuleCat.{u} R) ℕ}
    (φ : C ⟶ D) (hD : (D.sc 0).f = 0) [IsIso (HomologicalComplex.opcyclesMap φ 0)] :
    Function.Surjective (φ.f 0).hom := by
  intro y
  obtain ⟨z, hz⟩ := (ModuleCat.epi_iff_surjective
    (HomologicalComplex.opcyclesMap φ 0)).1 inferInstance (D.pOpcycles 0 y)
  obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := (ModuleCat.epi_iff_surjective (C.pOpcycles 0)).1 inferInstance z
  refine ⟨x, sub_eq_zero.mp (eq_zero_of_pOpcycles_eq_zero hD _ ?_)⟩
  have h1 := ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (HomologicalComplex.p_opcyclesMap φ 0) x
  simp only [ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, hx] at h1
  rw [map_sub, ← h1, hz, sub_self]

/-- A map of chain complexes onto a complex with zero differential into degree zero which is an
isomorphism on opcycles in degree zero makes `C₁ ⟶ C₀ ⟶ D₀` exact. -/
private theorem exact_f_zero_of_isIso_opcyclesMap {C D : ChainComplex (ModuleCat.{u} R) ℕ}
    (φ : C ⟶ D) (hD : (D.sc 0).f = 0) [IsIso (HomologicalComplex.opcyclesMap φ 0)] :
    Function.Exact ((C.sc 0).f).hom (φ.f 0).hom := by
  have hcomm := HomologicalComplex.p_opcyclesMap φ 0
  intro y
  constructor
  · intro hy
    have hp : C.pOpcycles 0 y = 0 := by
      refine (ModuleCat.mono_iff_injective
        (HomologicalComplex.opcyclesMap φ 0)).1 inferInstance ?_
      have key : (HomologicalComplex.opcyclesMap φ 0).hom ((C.pOpcycles 0).hom y) =
          (D.pOpcycles 0).hom ((φ.f 0).hom y) := ConcreteCategory.congr_hom hcomm y
      rw [show (φ.f 0).hom y = 0 from hy, map_zero] at key
      exact key.trans (map_zero _).symm
    obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ := (pOpcycles_eq_zero_iff_mem_range y).1 hp
    exact ⟨w, hw⟩
  · rintro ⟨w, rfl⟩
    have hcc := ((HomologicalComplex.shortComplexFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R)
      (ComplexShape.down ℕ) 0).map φ).comm₁₂
    rw [hD, comp_zero] at hcc
    exact ConcreteCategory.congr_hom hcc.symm w

/-- A map of chain complexes onto a complex with zero differential into degree zero which is
surjective in degree zero, with `C₁ ⟶ C₀ ⟶ D₀` exact, is an isomorphism on opcycles in degree
zero. -/
private theorem isIso_opcyclesMap_zero_of_exact {C D : ChainComplex (ModuleCat.{u} R) ℕ}
    (φ : C ⟶ D) (hD : (D.sc 0).f = 0) (hsurj : Function.Surjective (φ.f 0).hom)
    (hexact : Function.Exact ((C.sc 0).f).hom (φ.f 0).hom) :
    IsIso (HomologicalComplex.opcyclesMap φ 0) := by
  have : Epi (φ.f 0) := (ModuleCat.epi_iff_surjective _).2 hsurj
  have hmono : Mono (HomologicalComplex.opcyclesMap φ 0) := by
    rw [ModuleCat.mono_iff_injective]
    intro z z' hzz'
    have hsub : HomologicalComplex.opcyclesMap φ 0 (z - z') = 0 := by
      rw [map_sub, hzz', sub_self]
    obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := (ModuleCat.epi_iff_surjective (C.pOpcycles 0)).1 inferInstance (z - z')
    have h1 := ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (HomologicalComplex.p_opcyclesMap φ 0) x
    simp only [ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, hx] at h1
    have h2 : φ.f 0 x = 0 := eq_zero_of_pOpcycles_eq_zero hD _ (by rw [← h1, hsub])
    obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ := (hexact x).1 h2
    rw [← sub_eq_zero, ← hx, (pOpcycles_eq_zero_iff_mem_range x).2 ⟨w, hw⟩]
  exact isIso_of_mono_of_epi _

/-- **The augmentation of a chain complex onto a module placed in degree zero stays an
isomorphism on `H₀` after tensoring by a module.** In degree zero the homology of a chain complex
indexed by `ℕ` is the cokernel of the differential into degree zero, so the hypothesis says that
`C₁ ⟶ C₀ ⟶ Q ⟶ 0` is exact; tensoring is right exact, so that sequence tensored by `M` is exact
again, which is the conclusion. -/
theorem isIso_homologyMap_zero_rTensor (M : ModuleCat.{u} R)
    {C : ChainComplex (ModuleCat.{u} R) ℕ} {Q : ModuleCat.{u} R}
    (α : C ⟶ (ChainComplex.single₀ (ModuleCat.{u} R)).obj Q)
    (hα : IsIso (HomologicalComplex.homologyMap α 0)) :
    IsIso (HomologicalComplex.homologyMap ((rTensorChainFunctor M).map α) 0) := by
  have hLd : (((ChainComplex.single₀ (ModuleCat.{u} R)).obj Q).sc 0).f = 0 := rfl
  have : IsIso (HomologicalComplex.opcyclesMap α 0) := (isIso_opcyclesMap_zero_iff α).2 hα
  have hsurj := surjective_f_zero_of_isIso_opcyclesMap α hLd
  have hd : (((rTensorChainFunctor M).obj
      ((ChainComplex.single₀ (ModuleCat.{u} R)).obj Q)).sc 0).f = 0 := by
    change (rTensorFunctor M).map
      ((((ChainComplex.single₀ (ModuleCat.{u} R)).obj Q).sc 0).f) = 0
    rw [hLd, (rTensorFunctor M).map_zero]
  exact (isIso_opcyclesMap_zero_iff _).1 (isIso_opcyclesMap_zero_of_exact _ hd
    (LinearMap.rTensor_surjective M hsurj)
    (_root_.rTensor_exact M (exact_f_zero_of_isIso_opcyclesMap α hLd) hsurj))

/-! ### The two towers in the derived category, and the pro-isomorphism -/

/-- An additive functor carries a zero object to a zero object. -/
theorem isZero_rTensorFunctor_obj (M : ModuleCat.{u} R) {P : ModuleCat.{u} R} (h : IsZero P) :
    IsZero ((rTensorFunctor M).obj P) := by
  rw [IsZero.iff_id_eq_zero] at h ⊢
  rw [← (rTensorFunctor M).map_id, h, (rTensorFunctor M).map_zero]

/-- A chain complex, reindexed cohomologically, has no homology in a degree `i` whenever its terms
in the degree `-j` with `-j = i` vanish. -/
private theorem isZero_homology_extendDown_of_isZero_X {K : ChainComplex (ModuleCat.{u} R) ℕ}
    (i : ℤ) (h : ∀ j : ℕ, -(j : ℤ) = i → IsZero (K.X j)) :
    IsZero ((K.extend ComplexShape.embeddingDownNat).homology i) := by
  have hX : IsZero ((K.extend ComplexShape.embeddingDownNat).X i) := by
    by_cases hp : ∃ j : ℕ, -(j : ℤ) = i
    · obtain ⟨j, hj⟩ := hp
      exact (h j hj).of_iso (K.extendXIso ComplexShape.embeddingDownNat hj)
    · exact K.isZero_extend_X ComplexShape.embeddingDownNat i (fun j hj => hp ⟨j, hj⟩)
  exact (K.extend ComplexShape.embeddingDownNat).sc i |>.isZero_homology_of_isZero_X₂ hX

/-- The Koszul complex with coefficients, reindexed cohomologically, has no homology outside the
degrees `-r, …, 0`. -/
theorem coefficient_extendDown_isZero_homology_outside {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → R)
    (M : ModuleCat.{u} R) (i : ℤ) (hi : i < -(r : ℤ) ∨ 0 < i) :
    IsZero ((((rTensorChainFunctor M).obj (Koszul.seqComplex f)).extend
      ComplexShape.embeddingDownNat).homology i) :=
  isZero_homology_extendDown_of_isZero_X i fun j hj =>
    isZero_rTensorFunctor_obj M
      (koszul_seqComplex_isZero_X_of_gt f j (by rcases hi with hi | hi <;> omega))

/-- A module placed in degree zero and tensored by `M`, reindexed cohomologically, has no
homology outside degree zero. -/
theorem coefficient_single_extendDown_isZero_homology_of_ne_zero (Q M : ModuleCat.{u} R)
    (i : ℤ) (hi : i ≠ 0) :
    IsZero ((((rTensorChainFunctor M).obj
      ((ChainComplex.single₀ (ModuleCat.{u} R)).obj Q)).extend
        ComplexShape.embeddingDownNat).homology i) :=
  isZero_homology_extendDown_of_isZero_X i fun j hj =>
    isZero_rTensorFunctor_obj M
      (HomologicalComplex.isZero_single_obj_X (ComplexShape.down ℕ) 0 Q j (by omega))

/-- If the reindexed chain complex `K` has no homology in degree `i`, neither does its image in
the derived category. -/
private theorem isZero_homologyFunctor_Q_obj_extendDown {K : ChainComplex (ModuleCat.{u} R) ℕ}
    (i : ℤ) (h : IsZero ((K.extend ComplexShape.embeddingDownNat).homology i)) :
    IsZero ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) i).obj
      (DerivedCategory.Q.obj (K.extend ComplexShape.embeddingDownNat))) :=
  h.of_iso ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctorFactors (ModuleCat.{u} R) i).app _)

/-- **The Koszul tower with coefficients.** The inverse system in `D(R)` of the Koszul complexes
on the positive powers of `f`, tensored with `M`. Since the Koszul complexes are bounded complexes
of finite free modules, this computes `M ⊗^𝐋_R K(f₁ⁿ, …, f_rⁿ)`. -/
@[sga "2 II Lemma11" "partial", sga "2 II Lemma9" "more general"]
noncomputable def coefficientKoszulPowerSystem {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → R) (M : ModuleCat.{u} R) :
    ℕᵒᵖ ⥤ DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} R) :=
  Functor.ofOpSequence (X := fun n ↦ DerivedCategory.Q.obj
    (((rTensorChainFunctor M).obj (Koszul.seqComplex (fun i ↦ f i ^ (n + 1)))).extend
      ComplexShape.embeddingDownNat))
    (fun n ↦ DerivedCategory.Q.map
      (HomologicalComplex.extendMap
        ((rTensorChainFunctor M).map (koszulPowerTransition f (n + 1) n (Nat.le_succ n)))
        ComplexShape.embeddingDownNat))

/-- **The quotient tower with coefficients.** The inverse system in `D(R)` of the modules
`R / (f₁ⁿ, …, f_rⁿ)` tensored with `M`, placed in degree zero. -/
noncomputable def coefficientQuotientPowerSystem {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → R) (M : ModuleCat.{u} R) :
    ℕᵒᵖ ⥤ DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} R) :=
  Functor.ofOpSequence (X := fun n ↦ DerivedCategory.Q.obj
    (((rTensorChainFunctor M).obj ((ChainComplex.single₀ (ModuleCat.{u} R)).obj
      (ModuleCat.of R (R ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range fun i ↦ f i ^ (n + 1)))))).extend
        ComplexShape.embeddingDownNat))
    (fun n ↦ DerivedCategory.Q.map
      (HomologicalComplex.extendMap
        ((rTensorChainFunctor M).map ((ChainComplex.single₀ (ModuleCat.{u} R)).map
          (quotientPowerTransition f (n + 1) n (Nat.le_succ n))))
        ComplexShape.embeddingDownNat))

/-- The canonical comparison from the Koszul tower with coefficients to the quotient tower with
coefficients, induced levelwise by the Koszul augmentation. -/
noncomputable def coefficientKoszulQuotientComparison {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → R)
    (M : ModuleCat.{u} R) :
    coefficientKoszulPowerSystem f M ⟶ coefficientQuotientPowerSystem f M :=
  NatTrans.ofOpSequence
    (fun n ↦ DerivedCategory.Q.map
      (HomologicalComplex.extendMap
        ((rTensorChainFunctor M).map (Koszul.koszulAugmentation (fun i ↦ f i ^ (n + 1))))
        ComplexShape.embeddingDownNat))
    (fun n ↦ by
      have hchain : HomologicalComplex.extendMap ((rTensorChainFunctor M).map
              (koszulPowerTransition f (n + 1) n (Nat.le_succ n)))
              ComplexShape.embeddingDownNat ≫
            HomologicalComplex.extendMap ((rTensorChainFunctor M).map
              (Koszul.koszulAugmentation (fun i ↦ f i ^ (n + 1))))
              ComplexShape.embeddingDownNat =
          HomologicalComplex.extendMap ((rTensorChainFunctor M).map
              (Koszul.koszulAugmentation (fun i ↦ f i ^ (n + 1 + 1))))
              ComplexShape.embeddingDownNat ≫
            HomologicalComplex.extendMap ((rTensorChainFunctor M).map
              ((ChainComplex.single₀ (ModuleCat.{u} R)).map
                (quotientPowerTransition f (n + 1) n (Nat.le_succ n))))
              ComplexShape.embeddingDownNat := by
        rw [← HomologicalComplex.extendMap_comp, ← HomologicalComplex.extendMap_comp,
          ← (rTensorChainFunctor M).map_comp, ← (rTensorChainFunctor M).map_comp,
          koszulQuotientAugmentation_naturality]
      simp only [coefficientKoszulPowerSystem, coefficientQuotientPowerSystem,
        Functor.ofOpSequence_map_homOfLE_succ]
      exact ((DerivedCategory.Q.map_comp _ _).symm.trans
        (congrArg (fun φ ↦ DerivedCategory.Q.map φ) hchain)).trans
        (DerivedCategory.Q.map_comp _ _))

/-- Each component of the comparison is the image in the derived category of the Koszul
augmentation tensored with `M`. -/
theorem coefficientKoszulQuotientComparison_app {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → R) (M : ModuleCat.{u} R)
    (n : ℕ) :
    (coefficientKoszulQuotientComparison f M).app (op n) =
      DerivedCategory.Q.map (HomologicalComplex.extendMap
        ((rTensorChainFunctor M).map (Koszul.koszulAugmentation (fun i ↦ f i ^ (n + 1))))
        ComplexShape.embeddingDownNat) := rfl

/-- The Koszul tower with coefficients has no homology outside the degrees `-r, …, 0`. -/
theorem homologyFunctor_coefficientKoszulPowerSystem_isZero_outside {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → R)
    (M : ModuleCat.{u} R) (i : ℤ) (hi : i < -(r : ℤ) ∨ 0 < i) (n : ℕ) :
    IsZero ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) i).obj
      ((coefficientKoszulPowerSystem f M).obj (op n))) := by
  exact isZero_homologyFunctor_Q_obj_extendDown i
    (coefficient_extendDown_isZero_homology_outside (fun j => f j ^ (n + 1)) M i hi)

/-- The quotient tower with coefficients has no homology outside degree zero. -/
theorem homologyFunctor_coefficientQuotientPowerSystem_isZero_of_ne_zero {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → R)
    (M : ModuleCat.{u} R) (i : ℤ) (hi : i ≠ 0) (n : ℕ) :
    IsZero ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) i).obj
      ((coefficientQuotientPowerSystem f M).obj (op n))) := by
  exact isZero_homologyFunctor_Q_obj_extendDown i
    (coefficient_single_extendDown_isZero_homology_of_ne_zero _ M i hi)

/-- The transition maps of the Koszul tower with coefficients are the images in the derived
category of the Koszul transition maps tensored with `M`. -/
private theorem coefficientKoszulPowerSystem_map_homOfLE {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → R)
    (M : ModuleCat.{u} R) (m n : ℕ) (h : n ≤ m) :
    (coefficientKoszulPowerSystem f M).map (homOfLE h).op =
      DerivedCategory.Q.map (HomologicalComplex.extendMap
        ((rTensorChainFunctor M).map (koszulPowerTransition f m n h))
        ComplexShape.embeddingDownNat) := by
  induction m, h using Nat.le_induction with
  | base =>
      rw [koszulPowerTransition_id, (rTensorChainFunctor M).map_id]
      simp [coefficientKoszulPowerSystem]
      rfl
  | succ m hnm ih =>
      have hcat : (homOfLE (hnm.trans (Nat.le_succ m))).op =
          (homOfLE (Nat.le_succ m)).op ≫ (homOfLE hnm).op := Subsingleton.elim _ _
      rw [hcat, Functor.map_comp, ih]
      rw [show (coefficientKoszulPowerSystem f M).map (homOfLE (Nat.le_succ m)).op =
          DerivedCategory.Q.map (HomologicalComplex.extendMap
            ((rTensorChainFunctor M).map
              (koszulPowerTransition f (m + 1) m (Nat.le_succ m)))
            ComplexShape.embeddingDownNat) from
        Functor.ofOpSequence_map_homOfLE_succ _ m]
      have hchain : HomologicalComplex.extendMap ((rTensorChainFunctor M).map
            (koszulPowerTransition f (m + 1) m (Nat.le_succ m)))
            ComplexShape.embeddingDownNat ≫
          HomologicalComplex.extendMap ((rTensorChainFunctor M).map
            (koszulPowerTransition f m n hnm)) ComplexShape.embeddingDownNat =
        HomologicalComplex.extendMap ((rTensorChainFunctor M).map
          (koszulPowerTransition f (m + 1) n (hnm.trans (Nat.le_succ m))))
          ComplexShape.embeddingDownNat := by
        rw [← HomologicalComplex.extendMap_comp, ← (rTensorChainFunctor M).map_comp,
          koszulPowerTransition_comp]
      exact (DerivedCategory.Q.map_comp _ _).symm.trans
        (congrArg (fun φ ↦ DerivedCategory.Q.map φ) hchain)

/-- **The negative cohomology of the Koszul tower with coefficients is pro-zero.** -/
theorem homologyFunctor_coefficientKoszulPowerSystem_transition_eq_zero_neg
    [IsNoetherianRing R] {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → R) (M : ModuleCat.{u} R) [Module.Finite R M]
    (i : ℤ) (hi : i < 0) (n : ℕ) :
    ∃ (m : ℕ) (h : n ≤ m),
      (DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) i).map
        ((coefficientKoszulPowerSystem f M).map (homOfLE h).op) = 0 := by
  let j : ℕ := (-i).toNat
  have hj : 0 < j := by
    dsimp [j]
    omega
  have hji : i = -(j : ℤ) := by
    dsimp [j]
    omega
  obtain ⟨m, h, hzero⟩ := koszulCoefficientTransition_homologyMap_eq_zero_pos f M n j hj
  refine ⟨m, h, ?_⟩
  rw [hji, coefficientKoszulPowerSystem_map_homOfLE]
  exact homologyFunctor_Q_map_eq_zero_of_homologyMap_eq_zero _ _
    (homologyMap_extendDown_eq_zero_of_homologyMap_eq_zero _ j hzero)

/-- **In degree zero the comparison with coefficients is an isomorphism.** -/
theorem homologyFunctor_coefficientKoszulQuotientComparison_isIso_zero {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → R)
    (M : ModuleCat.{u} R) (n : ℕ) :
    IsIso ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) 0).map
      ((coefficientKoszulQuotientComparison f M).app (op n))) := by
  rw [coefficientKoszulQuotientComparison_app]
  let α := (rTensorChainFunctor M).map (Koszul.koszulAugmentation (fun i ↦ f i ^ (n + 1)))
  have h0 : IsIso (HomologicalComplex.homologyMap α 0) :=
    isIso_homologyMap_zero_rTensor M _ (koszulPowerAugmentation_homologyMap_zero_isIso f n)
  have h1 : IsIso (HomologicalComplex.homologyMap
      (HomologicalComplex.extendMap α ComplexShape.embeddingDownNat) (-((0 : ℕ) : ℤ))) :=
    homologyMap_extendDown_isIso_of_homologyMap_isIso α 0
  rw [Nat.cast_zero, neg_zero] at h1
  exact homologyFunctor_Q_map_isIso_of_homologyMap_isIso
    (HomologicalComplex.extendMap α ComplexShape.embeddingDownNat) 0

/-- **Stacks 0921 with coefficients, at an arbitrary number of generators.** Over a Noetherian
ring, for a finite module `M` and a finite sequence `f`, the inverse systems of `D(R)` formed by
the Koszul complexes on the positive powers of `f` tensored with `M` and by the quotients
`M ⊗_R R/(f₁ⁿ, …, f_rⁿ)` placed in degree zero are isomorphic as pro-objects: the comparison is a
natural transformation, and at every level it admits an inverse after passing to a later level.

This is the affine-local content of the pro-isomorphism used in the proof of
[Stacks, Tag 0A0K] part (1), at an arbitrary `r`: the tower on the left is
`n ↦ M ⊗^𝐋_R K(R, f₁ⁿ, …, f_rⁿ)`, because the Koszul complexes are bounded complexes of finite
free modules. -/
theorem coefficientKoszulPowerSystem_proIso_quotientPowerSystem [IsNoetherianRing R]
    {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → R) (M : ModuleCat.{u} R) [Module.Finite R M] :
    ∀ n : ℕ, ∃ (m : ℕ) (h : n ≤ m)
      (s : (coefficientQuotientPowerSystem f M).obj (op m) ⟶
        (coefficientKoszulPowerSystem f M).obj (op n)),
      (coefficientKoszulQuotientComparison f M).app (op m) ≫ s =
          (coefficientKoszulPowerSystem f M).map (homOfLE h).op ∧
        s ≫ (coefficientKoszulQuotientComparison f M).app (op n) =
          (coefficientQuotientPowerSystem f M).map (homOfLE h).op := by
  intro n
  let α := coefficientKoszulQuotientComparison f M
  let H := DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R)
  have hA (i : ℤ) (hi : i < -(r : ℤ) ∨ 0 < i) (j : ℕᵒᵖ) :
      IsZero ((H i).obj ((coefficientKoszulPowerSystem f M).obj j)) :=
    homologyFunctor_coefficientKoszulPowerSystem_isZero_outside f M i hi j.unop
  have hB (i : ℤ) (hi : i < -(r : ℤ) ∨ 0 < i) (j : ℕᵒᵖ) :
      IsZero ((H i).obj ((coefficientQuotientPowerSystem f M).obj j)) :=
    homologyFunctor_coefficientQuotientPowerSystem_isZero_of_ne_zero f M i (by omega) j.unop
  have hH (i : ℤ) (j : ℕᵒᵖ) :
      ∃ (k : ℕᵒᵖ) (g : k ⟶ j)
        (s : (H i).obj ((coefficientQuotientPowerSystem f M).obj k) ⟶
          (H i).obj ((coefficientKoszulPowerSystem f M).obj j)),
        (H i).map (α.app k) ≫ s =
          (H i).map ((coefficientKoszulPowerSystem f M).map g) ∧
          s ≫ (H i).map (α.app j) =
          (H i).map ((coefficientQuotientPowerSystem f M).map g) := by
    rcases lt_trichotomy i 0 with hin | rfl | hip
    · obtain ⟨m, h, hzero⟩ :=
        homologyFunctor_coefficientKoszulPowerSystem_transition_eq_zero_neg f M i hin j.unop
      exact ⟨op m, (homOfLE h).op, 0, by simpa using hzero.symm,
        (homologyFunctor_coefficientQuotientPowerSystem_isZero_of_ne_zero f M i hin.ne
          m).eq_of_src _ _⟩
    · have : IsIso ((H 0).map (α.app j)) :=
        homologyFunctor_coefficientKoszulQuotientComparison_isIso_zero f M j.unop
      exact ⟨j, 𝟙 j, inv ((H 0).map (α.app j)), by simp, by simp⟩
    · exact ⟨j, 𝟙 j, 0, (hA i (Or.inr hip) j).eq_of_tgt _ _,
        (hB i (Or.inr hip) j).eq_of_src _ _⟩
  obtain ⟨k, g, s, hs₁, hs₂⟩ :=
    DerivedCategory.exists_proInverse_of_proInverse_homology α (-(r : ℤ)) 0 hA hB hH (op n)
  have h : n ≤ k.unop := leOfHom g.unop
  have hg : g = (homOfLE h).op := Subsingleton.elim _ _
  refine ⟨k.unop, h, s, ?_, ?_⟩
  · simpa [α, hg] using hs₁
  · simpa [α, hg] using hs₂

end Stacks.KoszulCoefficientProIso

